<header class="about-hero">
 <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE PROJECT</p>
 <h1>About Sherubtse TripHub</h1>
 <p class="lead">Sherubtse TripHub is a student-focused trip planning and management platform developed for the Sherubtse College community in Kanglung, Bhutan.</p>
 <p>This project supports students and the college's trip review process with one place to prepare proposals, organize participation, and keep trip information together.</p>
</header>
<section class="section-block about-purpose" aria-labelledby="purpose-heading">
 <div><p class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE</p><h2 id="purpose-heading">Make each stage easier to follow</h2></div>
 <p>TripHub helps students prepare clear proposals and helps the Dean of Student Affairs review them. Once a proposal is approved, assigned Student Coordinators can manage registration and trip operations while participants receive the information they need.</p>
</section>
<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
 <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE DO</p><h2 id="what-heading">Support the full trip lifecycle</h2></div><p>Every stage has a clear owner and review point.</p></div>
 <div class="about-work-grid">
  <article class="about-work-card"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Prepare and review</h3><p>Students submit trip proposals. DSA reviews each proposal and assigns a lead Coordinator and, when needed, assistants.</p></article>
  <article class="about-work-card"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Register and consent</h3><p>After approval, assigned Coordinators open registration, review participation requests, and manage parent or guardian consent documents.</p></article>
  <article class="about-work-card"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Clear and complete</h3><p>The lead submits the final participant list and consent package for DSA approval before departure. TripHub also supports trip coordination and completion records.</p></article>
 </div>
</section>
<section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="roles-heading">
 <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHO USES TRIPHUB</p><h2 id="roles-heading">One community, clear responsibilities</h2></div></div>
 <div class="about-role-grid">
  <article class="about-role-card"><span class="about-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">S</span><h3>Students</h3><p>Discover approved trips, prepare proposals, request to participate, and manage their own trip information.</p></article>
  <article class="about-role-card"><span class="about-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">C</span><h3>Trip Coordinators</h3><p>Students with an active, trip-specific assignment who manage that trip's registration and operations.</p></article>
  <article class="about-role-card"><span class="about-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">D</span><h3>DSA</h3><p>Reviews trip proposals, assigns Coordinators, and approves final participant lists and consent packages.</p></article>
  <article class="about-role-card"><span class="about-role-icon" aria-hidden="true">A</span><h3>Superadmin</h3><p>Manages the platform and its general content. Superadmin does not replace DSA trip approval or Coordinator assignment.</p></article>
 </div>
</section>
<section class="section-block about-process" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
 <p class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</p><h2 id="process-heading">From proposal to departure</h2>
 <ol class="about-steps">
  <li><span>1</span><strong>Student proposes a trip</strong></li>
  <li><span>2</span><strong>DSA reviews and approves</strong></li>
  <li><span>3</span><strong>Coordinator manages registration</strong></li>
  <li><span>4</span><strong>Students request to join and submit consent</strong></li>
  <li><span>5</span><strong>DSA approves the final namelist</strong></li>
  <li><span>6</span><strong>The trip takes place</strong></li>
 </ol>
</section>
<aside class="about-notice" aria-label="Institutional notice"><span aria-hidden="true">i</span><p><strong>Project notice</strong><br>Sherubtse TripHub is a student-developed project and does not imply official Sherubtse College endorsement. TripHub does not replace DSA permission, signed forms, or other institutional requirements.</p></aside>
